{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"ALSA-2026:89747","published":"2026-10-26T00:00:00Z","modified":"2026-10-26T11:27:01.045912284Z","related":["CVE-2026-88812","CVE-2026-93516","CVE-2026-93517","CVE-2026-93518","CVE-2026-93519","CVE-2026-93520","CVE-2026-93521","CVE-2026-93523"],"summary":"Important: xorg-x11-server security update","details":"X.Org is an open-source implementation of the X Window System. It provides the basic low-level functionality that full-fledged graphical user interfaces are designed upon.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * xorg-x11-server: xorg-x11-server: Arbitrary code execution via use-after-free in passive grab handling (CVE-2026-93516)\n  * xorg-x11-server: xorg-x11-server: Privilege escalation via crafted RandR provider property requests (CVE-2026-93521)\n  * xorg-x11-server: xwayland: xorg-x11-server: Arbitrary code execution via double-free in XKB geometry handling (CVE-2026-88812)\n  * xorg-x11-server: xorg-x11-server: Out-of-bounds write via unvalidated modifier in ProcXIPassiveUngrabDevice (CVE-2026-93523)\n  * xorg-x11-server: xorg-x11-server: arbitrary code execution via GLX RenderLarge heap-based buffer overflow (CVE-2026-93517)\n  * xorg-x11-server: xorg-x11-server: arbitrary code execution via integer truncation during keyboard mapping resize (CVE-2026-93518)\n  * xorg-x11-server: xorg-x11-server: Arbitrary code execution via buffer overflow in input_constrain_cursor() (CVE-2026-93519)\n  * xorg-x11-server: xorg-x11-server: arbitrary code execution via out-of-bounds write in XKB keycode handling (CVE-2026-93520)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"xorg-x11-server-Xdmx","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/xorg-x11-server-Xdmx"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.20.11-28.el8_10.5"}]}],"database